course: dictionary
lesson: 14449
title: Parachutist
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A parachutist is a person who jumps from an aircraft and floats down using a parachute. The word is built from parts you may know: «para» means protect, and «chute» is short for parachute. «The parachutist jumped out of the plane and floated down to the field.» The clues are plane, jumped and floated down, so a parachutist is someone who jumps from a plane and drifts to the ground.
explain: Science gives the word another meaning. An open parachute pushes against the air, and this is called air resistance. «The parachute opened, and the parachutist fell more slowly.» The parachute slows the fall because it pushes against the air.
explain: In history, soldiers called paratroopers jumped from planes into battles, and they are a kind of parachutist. In sport, people do parachute jumps and skydives for fun or to raise money for charity. Check the context to see which meaning the writer wants.
fact: A parachutist is a person who jumps from an aircraft and floats down using a parachute.
fact: «Parachutist» comes from «parachute», and the two words are closely linked.
fact: An open parachute pushes against the air, which slows the fall. This is air resistance.
fact: In history, paratroopers were parachutists who jumped into battles.
fact: People also do parachute jumps and skydives for sport and charity.
exercise: «The parachutist jumped out of the plane and floated down to the field.» What is a parachutist? | A bird that glides on the wind | *A person who jumps from an aircraft and floats down with a parachute | A pilot who flies the plane | A rope used to climb a tree
exercise: In science, «the parachute opened, and the parachutist fell more slowly.» What does the parachute push against to slow the fall? | The ground | The plane | *The air | The clouds
exercise: Find and copy the word from this sentence that means a flying machine: «The parachutist jumped out of the plane.» | jumped | parachutist | out | *plane
test: «The parachutists landed safely in the field after their charity skydive.» What were the parachutists doing? | *Jumping from an aircraft with parachutes for charity | Walking home from school | Flying the plane | Digging a hole in the field
test: In history, «paratroopers were parachutists who jumped into battles.» Which idea fits best? | *Paratroopers were soldiers who jumped from planes using parachutes | Paratroopers were fish that swam in rivers | Paratroopers were teachers in schools | Paratroopers were kinds of cloud
exam: Which sentence uses «parachutist» correctly? | The parachutist read a book about dinosaurs | *The parachutist floated safely to the ground after jumping from the plane | The parachutist swam across the lake to school | The parachutist baked a cake for the class
